{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Preadditive"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.dichotomy_of_scalars_field","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.dichotomy_of_scalars_field","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy.lean#L151-L171","doc":"**No non-trivial model, when the scalars form a field.**\n\nThe hypothesis `hscal` is exactly \"`End (𝟙_C)` has no non-zero\nnon-invertible element\", which holds in `ModuleCat k` for `k` a field and in\nany `k`-linear category with simple unit. It is taken as a hypothesis rather\nthan derived from a field instance so that the statement applies wherever\nthe disjunction does.\n\nThe conclusion: `A` is a zero object, or a retract of `𝟙_C`. There is no\nthird case, and in particular no non-trivial substrate.\n\n**This is the negative answer to bean `qou-aawz`** in the linear setting. It\nis silent about a bare monoidal category, where `σ = 0` is not statable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.id_eq_zero_of_unitCounit_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.id_eq_zero_of_unitCounit_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy.lean#L138-L147","doc":"**`A` is a zero object** whenever the scalar `ε(1)` vanishes.\n\n`𝟙_A = 0`, which in any category with zero morphisms makes `A` a zero\nobject. Additivity of whiskering is the only extra ingredient; no\nlinearity, no field, no antipode beyond what\n`scalar_id_eq_counit_unit` already spent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.retract_of_unit_of_isIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.retract_of_unit_of_isIso","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy.lean#L123-L134","doc":"**`A` is a retract of the tensor unit** whenever `ε(1)` is invertible.\n\nThe splitting is `A --ε--> 𝟙_C --η ≫ (ε ≫ η)⁻¹--> A`.\n\nIn `ModuleCat k` the unit is `k`, whose only retracts are `0` and `k`, so\nthis says `A` is at most one-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.isIso_counit_comp_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.isIso_counit_comp_unit","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy.lean#L110-L121","doc":"If the scalar `σ = η ≫ ε` is invertible, so is `ε ≫ η`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.id_factors_through_unitCounit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.id_factors_through_unitCounit","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy.lean#L94-L106","doc":"**The identity on `A` factors through the scalar `σ = η ≫ ε`.**\n\nSubstituting `scalar_id_eq_counit_unit` into `frobeniusLoop_counit_unit`.\nNo hypothesis beyond the structure's own fields.\n\nRead in elements: `x = ε(1) · (μ ∘ Δ)(x)`. So the whole identity morphism\nis `ε(1)` times something, which is what makes both branches of the\ndichotomy below work. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusLoop_counit_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.frobeniusLoop_counit_unit","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy.lean#L83-L92","doc":"**The Frobenius loop with `ε ≫ η` inserted is the identity.**\n\n`Δ ≫ (A ◁ (ε ≫ η)) ≫ μ = 𝟙_A`, in elements `Σ ε(x₂)·x₁ = x`.\n\nThis uses only the right counit law and the right unit law — **no antipode\naxiom** — so it holds of any Frobenius object whatever its `S`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}